  "author_overlap": "Author of new adapter successor and historical point/engine/primitive ancestry. ea300 parent implementation authored by Diagnosis; independent marked verifier by Diagnosis, decorator by Controls. This is author static evidence, not an independent self-review. Root owns future composition/grants/actuals.",
  "change": "Private _filter_all_checked keeps every inherited check, returning local already-checked full tiles in original order including removed ones. Existing _filter pair wrapper and all public proposal/receipt/EOF/transition/state fields remain exact. Cursor uses those tiles only for unchanged persistent both-ID full-preimage collision census instead of rebuilding them again.",
  "value_equivalence_argument": [
    "Inherited _filter already reconstructs bare original tile, validates original whole legality and complete raw packet, rebuilds full marked tile with fresh independent verifier9fd, checks collisions/unique keys and full point legality or actual channel4 conflict. No original candidate may reach all_checked without these checks succeeding.",
    "All those operations remain in the factored core in the same order; erasing only the local list/append/triple and restoring name is exact old whole AST. The public pair is exactly inherited checked/removed.",
    "Old advance immediately rebuilt the same preimage/translation under the same frozen marking/private language only for check_collision. Under pinned synchronous unchanged Sources, it yields identical original/decorated full type key/preimage; new advance uses these already checked values for the same ledger. No native receipt is copied/relabelled as independently recomputed.",
    "with_obligations only adds unchanged read metadata to surviving tile object. Persistent collision consumes base_tile placement key and decorated placement key/fullpreimages, which remain unchanged. Removed tile remains available to the persistent census; no omission of prior-removed/prototype collisions.",
    "Native/parser visit/tick/resource prefixes can differ because a duplicate reconstruction was removed and a native census-entry tick remains. No nth-tick, interruption point, complete runtime bytes, timing gain or fit equivalence is claimed. Source alone qualifies no execution."
  ],
  "ownership_and_failure_scope": {
    "local_only": "all_checked list exists only in current _filter wrapper/advance stack; no self/cache/cursor context/receipt field added. Cursor singleton original filter call has one reference, generic list filter has one reference per input.",
    "shared_survivor": "Private list and ordinary checked survivor may alias same tile; only collision read happens before ordinary result copy. No mutation/delegation is introduced between filter and census under trusted pinned Sources.",
    "removed": "Every removed tile still receives persistent original+decorated collision check before raw/removed counters advance, exactly inherited ordering.",
    "exceptions": "Inherited full errors propagate; advance preserves BaseException poisoning, abort remains exact, no candidate-removal/fakeEOF/error-as-negative shortcut.",
    "authority": "All Root Source/call guards, full independent 9fd/c354/native membership/state/marking checks and engine fresh returned-candidate checks remain required. No shared proposer/checker/crosscall state or arbitrary mutable callback equivalence."
